.TH "DOCUMENTPICTUREINPICTURE.WINDOW" "3JS" "April 25, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
DocumentPictureInPicture.window \- DocumentPictureInPicture: window
property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]window\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]DocumentPictureInPicture\f[R] interface returns a
\f[CR]Window\f[R] instance representing the browsing context inside the
Picture\-in\-Picture window.
.SH VALUE
A \f[CR]Window\f[R] object instance if the Picture\-in\-Picture window
has already been opened using
\f[CR]DocumentPictureInPicture.requestWindow()\f[R], or \f[CR]null\f[R]
otherwise.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] videoPlayer = document.getElementById(\(dqplayer\(dq);

\f[I]// \&...\f[R]

\f[B]await\f[R] window.documentPictureInPicture.requestWindow({
  width: videoPlayer.clientWidth,
  height: videoPlayer.clientHeight,
});

\f[I]// \&...\f[R]

\f[B]const\f[R] pipWindow = window.documentPictureInPicture.window;
\f[B]if\f[R] (pipWindow) {
  \f[I]// Mute video playing in the Picture\-in\-Picture window.\f[R]
  \f[B]const\f[R] pipVideo = pipWindow.document.querySelector(\(dq#video\(dq);
  pipVideo.muted = \f[B]true\f[R];
}
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Document Picture\-in\-Picture API
.IP \(bu 2
Using the Document Picture\-in\-Picture API
